<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Curriculum sub-strand: Core 2.1 -->

<chapter xml:id="ch-matrices-and-transformations" component="core" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Matrices and Transformations</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      In Grade <m>11</m> you learned to add and multiply matrices and to find the determinant and the inverse of a <m>2 \times 2</m> matrix. In earlier grades you also reflected, rotated, enlarged and translated shapes on the Cartesian plane.
    </p>
    <p>
      This chapter brings the two ideas together. You will use a <m>2 \times 2</m> matrix to transform an object and find the matrix for a given transformation. You will combine successive transformations into a single matrix, undo a transformation with the inverse matrix, and relate the determinant to the area scale factor. You will also meet two new transformations, stretch and shear, before applying matrices of transformation to different situations.
    </p>
    <p>
      Matrices of transformation are behind computer graphics, animation and the design software that architects and engineers use.
    </p>
  </introduction>

